Some people claim that what exists, 
is a vector in Configuration space. 
What we experience, is a current state,
an operator and a predicted probability
distribution of the next state. 
Or we experience a current state, 
a memory of a previous state 
and a memory of an operator that
predicted how likely it was that we got
the current state or any other. 
We see, state, prediction and result all
in one instant of experience, along
with any error valuation of the
prediction. 
In reinforcment learning, the agent
sees the state (which can be a rich
context of history), it applies its
operator and outputs a probability
distribution of the next action to take
(or token to write). This seems very 
analogous to quantum measurement.
The state vector is in
the embedding space. 
The output is not a 
probability distribution over
embedding space, but over
token space.
perhaps this is like an
individual measurment.
It defines the embedding
space distribution.

